A||N||7||RoadRocket||Installing Seat Covers||||5||
Z||000000||RoadRocket||09-29-2001||03:55 PM||||I just got some nice new seat covers, and then tried to install them the stupid way.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> At least, I think it is the stupid way...<P>The top portion of the seat cover went on without a hitch. The bottom, however, I could not put on, simply because there was not enough space underneath the seat to fasten the lower cover together.<P>So, now I'm thinking I may have to remove the seats entirely to get the covers installed.<P>What's the best way to remove the seats from my Fiero, I'm not totally sure, but I think it is the only way to get the lower cover on.<P>Unless someone's got a better idea.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||5
Z||000001||mbramble||09-29-2001||04:16 PM||||Are you talking about 'generic' seat covers that you buy from an auto store or replacement upholstery for the seats??<P>Anyway, to take the seats out there are 4 nuts, one under each corner of the seat that need to be removed.  Then just lift the seat out.  15mm nuts, I believe thought they could be 13mm....||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroFanaticus2||09-29-2001||04:33 PM||||The first set of seat cover I bought I did not take the seats out to put them on and the bottom part kept coming loose and crumpling up under my butt.  Those were just some cheap k-mart covers.  Then Later on I bought some more expensive covers and took the seats out so I could tie the cover retaining straps together under the seat.  It was kind of difficult at first because there is not much room between the seat and the metal rails, except for a small crack right about in the middle of them.  I got 'em on the way I wanted them and haven't had a problem since.  In my opinion, you will be happer with the end result if you remove the seats.  Now I get to pull the seats out again to install new carpet and then put on some Mr. Mikes Seats.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||RoadRocket||09-30-2001||11:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mbramble:<BR><B>Are you talking about 'generic' seat covers that you buy from an auto store or replacement upholstery for the seats??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm talkin' seat covers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000004||RoadRocket||09-30-2001||11:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroFanaticus2:<BR><B>It was kind of difficult at first because there is not much room between the seat and the metal rails, except for a small crack right about in the middle of them.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>That's exactly the problem I'm facing. And definately, I'm gonna have to remove the seats.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroFanaticus2||09-30-2001||11:56 AM||||I had to use a bent Metal Wire Clothes Hanger to help guide the straps through that little crack.||||reg||1
Z||000006||RoadRocket||09-30-2001||06:37 PM||||Mission Accomplished!<P>After much weeping and wailing and gnashing of teeth, I got them stinkin' covers on my seat.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroFanaticus2:<BR><B>I had to use a bent Metal Wire Clothes Hanger to help guide the straps through that little crack.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yea, I had to do that both times. First, when I tried putting the seat covers on without removing the seat, second after I removed them.<P>Somehow, I think retrieving the head of Osana *****  Laden would have been easier.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
